description:
**Your role, your impact**
As a Senior Trade & Logistics Consultant, you’ll play a critical role in delivering expert-level functional consulting services across Microsoft Dynamics 365 Finance & Operations (D365 F&O), with a focus on supply chain execution, procurement, sourcing, inventory management, landed cost, and global trade compliance. You’ll leverage your supply chain and Dynamics expertise to design and implement end-to-end trade and logistics solutions aligned with client operational goals, business requirements, and established delivery methodologies.


Your ability to lead supply chain discovery, translate complex logistics requirements into effective D365 F&O solutions, guide clients through implementation best practices, and mentor consulting teams will directly contribute to successful implementations, client confidence, and delivery excellence.




**Your day-to-day**

* Design end-to-end trade and logistics functional solutions that address complex supply chain requirements using D365 F&O;
* Lead and facilitate procurement, sourcing, logistics, and global trade business process discovery and requirements workshops;
* Perform gap analysis between client logistics processes and D365 F&O capabilities and recommend appropriate solutions;
* Configure D365 F&O supply chain modules including Procurement & Sourcing, Inventory Management, Landed Cost, and Global Trade;
* Review solution design recommendations and guide clients through implementation best practices, applying Microsoft Success by Design principles and established delivery methodologies;
* Develop functional design documents (FDDs) for custom developments, integrations, label printing, and ISV extensions;
* Design, develop, and execute SIT and UAT scenarios, and coordinate supply chain data migration activities including items, vendors, customers, on-hand inventory, open purchase orders, open sales orders, and trade agreements;
* Advise clients on solution roadmaps, upgrade paths, and ISV or third-party logistics extensions, and requirements for complex multi-site, multi-warehouse, and multi-country environments;
* Provide leadership and mentorship to consultants, support issue resolution, escalation management, and change control governance across supply chain workstreams;
* Contribute to project planning activities through effort estimation and maintain strong client relationships through delivery excellence.



**Keys to your success**

* Bachelor’s or advanced degree in Supply Chain Management, Logistics, Business Administration, Industrial Engineering, Information Systems, or a related field;
* Minimum 5 years of combined ERP and supply chain/logistics industry experience, including at least 3 years as a Dynamics D365 F&O consultant specializing in trade and logistics;
* Strong implementation experience across D365 F&O supply chain functionality, including Procurement & Sourcing, Inventory Management, Landed Cost, and Global Trade;
* Experience supporting multi-site, multi-warehouse, international trade implementations, distribution, industrial, MRO, spare parts, retail, 3PL, or consumer goods environments;
* Strong understanding of supply chain and logistics processes across procurement, sourcing, inventory, warehousing, transportation, landed cost, and global trade;
* Ability to conduct effective discovery sessions with diverse supply chain stakeholders including warehouse teams, traffic managers, import/export coordinators, buyers, and executive supply chain leaders;
* Strong understanding of project methodologies, change control processes, and delivery standards, with the ability to manage multiple supply chain workstreams within project schedules and budget constraints;
* Strong analytical, problem-solving, decision-making, communication, and collaboration skills, with the ability to present complex supply chain concepts to operational and executive stakeholders and work effectively across functional, technical, and integration teams.

**Extra edge**

* APICS CSCP, CLTD, or equivalent supply chain certification;
* Experience with Microsoft Success by Design, ISV and third-party logistics extensions, continuous improvement initiatives, and mentoring junior or mid-level D365 F&O consultants.

**Language Skills**

* English: Advanced



**Our mission, your future**
As a global network of trusted advisors, we create cutting-edge technological solutions to overcome today’s challenges and anticipate tomorrow’s needs. It all starts with the collaboration of a diverse team of passionate innovators, each driven to make a difference. Together, we challenge the status quo and push each other to new heights.


Ready to leave your mark on engaging mandates and shape the future through digital transformation and strategic consulting? Take your ambitions to the next level and discover your next exciting challenge with us!




**Our offer**

* Global collaboration: Partner directly with our North American teams on projects for clients in high-impact industries, gaining the kind of cross-border exposure that sharpens your expertise and expands your horizons.
* Continuous growth and learning: Unlimited access to online learning, plus certification paths, including through our Microsoft, Oracle, and Salesforce partnerships, so your expertise keeps pace with the technology you work on.
* Flexible work options: Work arrangements that support your rhythm and your reality.
* Support for your well-being: Comprehensive insurance plan to support you and your family, with premiums fully paid by us.

**Our commitments**

* Our authenticity is our strength: The diversity of our backgrounds, experiences, thoughts and insights is our competitive advantage. We foster a collaborative environment where we embrace our authenticity and leverage our unique perspectives to collectively build the future we all envision.
* An inclusive path to success: Fostering an environment where you can thrive starts with ensuring an accessible recruitment process. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to contact us. For more information, please visit our accessibility page: https://www.alithya.com/en/accessibility .
